      "cr": 0.5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — The Hallway Guard.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 1/2 as a soldier. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The One Who Counted the Wounds</strong> — Household of the Overgrown Manor</p><p>Status: Active - still standing in the hallway he was told to guard</p><p>A house guard left holding a corridor, and the only witness in the manor to notice that the reinforcements who died in it were not killed by plants. They had sword slashes. He is also the man who suggested putting the kitchen's soup inside a bomb, which is the best tactical idea anybody has had in this house.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Sabre</strong> — “They had sword slashes.”</li><li><strong>Cooks for an Army</strong> — “Told that Red's cooking withers the plants on contact, he asked the obvious question that four adventurers had failed to ask in two days: why not put the soup in a bomb?”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/the_hallway_reinforcement_guard</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/the_hallway_reinforcement_guard</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
